# Cloudflare Pages headers for NABL Tools (https://tools.nabl.in)
#
# Cloudflare Pages merges headers from every matching block (broadest to
# most specific, in file order) rather than letting a more specific path
# "win" automatically — if two matching blocks set the same header name,
# their values get comma-joined, which corrupts a structured header like
# Content-Security-Policy or Permissions-Policy. So every path-specific
# block below that needs a *different* CSP or Permissions-Policy than /*
# first detaches it with "! Header-Name" and then sets its own value.
# See qa/lighthouse-summary.md and the audit report for how these were
# derived and tested.

/*
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), display-capture=(), geolocation=(), payment=()
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; img-src 'self' data: blob:; media-src 'self' blob:; font-src 'self' data:; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' 'wasm-unsafe-eval'; worker-src 'self' blob:; connect-src 'self'; manifest-src 'self'

# Every built asset gets Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy AND
# Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy. Both are required for the COOP/COEP pages
# below — tested live (upload a file, click the action button, watch
# network requests) and found that Video Compressor's self-hosted ffmpeg
# worker script (/_astro/worker-*.js) failed with ERR_BLOCKED_BY_RESPONSE
# under COEP with only one of the two set: Chrome's require-corp blocks any
# response without a CORP header (even same-origin), AND separately requires
# a Worker's own script response to carry its own COEP header before the
# worker is allowed to load under a COEP-enabled page. With both headers
# here, the ffmpeg worker (and onnxruntime-web's worker, for the two ONNX
# tool pages below) load cleanly — re-verified with the same live test.
# Harmless on every other page too, since nothing here is meant to be
# embedded by a different origin anyway.
/_astro/*
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp

# Background Remover and Image Upscaler fetch their ONNX model weights from
# Hugging Face at runtime, and their onnxruntime-web WASM backend from
# jsdelivr (see src/tools/remove-background/onnxSetup.ts and
# src/tools/image-upscaler/onnxSetup.ts — the largest threaded WASM build is
# ~28MB, over Cloudflare's 25 MiB per-asset deploy limit, so it can't be
# bundled and is loaded from the CDN instead). Also scoped with COOP/COEP:
# both tools' onnxruntime-web falls back to non-threaded WASM today, but
# cross-origin isolation unlocks the threaded build later, and jsdelivr
# serves with CORS (satisfying COEP:require-corp without a separate CORP
# header).
#
# `blob:` in script-src is required (not just worker-src): onnxruntime-web
# fetches its .mjs core from wasmPaths as text, wraps it in a `blob:` URL,
# and dynamically `import()`s that blob — which is governed by script-src,
# same as the toBlobURL() pattern used for ffmpeg on /video-compressor/*.
# Without it, every InferenceSession.create() call fails with "no available
# backend found. ERR: [wasm] Error: previous call to 'initWasm()' failed." —
# reproduced locally against a local mock of jsdelivr (real jsdelivr is
# blocked by this sandbox's network policy) with the CSP below exactly as
# shipped, both with and without this fix, to isolate the cause.
/remove-background/*
  ! Content-Security-Policy
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; img-src 'self' data: blob:; media-src 'self' blob:; font-src 'self' data:; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' 'wasm-unsafe-eval' blob: https://cdn.jsdelivr.net; worker-src 'self' blob: https://cdn.jsdelivr.net; connect-src 'self' https://huggingface.co https://*.hf.co https://cdn.jsdelivr.net; manifest-src 'self'
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp

/image-upscaler/*
  ! Content-Security-Policy
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; img-src 'self' data: blob:; media-src 'self' blob:; font-src 'self' data:; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' 'wasm-unsafe-eval' blob: https://cdn.jsdelivr.net; worker-src 'self' blob: https://cdn.jsdelivr.net; connect-src 'self' https://huggingface.co https://*.hf.co https://cdn.jsdelivr.net; manifest-src 'self'
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp

# Video Compressor: the ffmpeg.wasm worker script itself stays self-hosted
# (own /_astro/* bundle, see that block above), but its ~30MB core (JS+WASM)
# is loaded from jsdelivr at runtime via toBlobURL() instead of being
# bundled — a bundled copy exceeds Cloudflare's 25 MiB per-asset deploy
# limit (see src/tools/video-compressor/ffmpegEngine.ts). jsdelivr serves
# with CORS (Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *), which satisfies COEP:
# require-corp for the fetch without needing a Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy
# response header, and toBlobURL's resulting blob: URL needs 'blob:' added
# to script-src to be import()-able. COOP/COEP is kept here so a future
# switch to the multithreaded @ffmpeg/core-mt build can use
# SharedArrayBuffer. NOT re-verified live post-change (jsdelivr is blocked
# in this sandbox's network policy) — confirm self.crossOriginIsolated and
# zero blocked requests on first real deploy.
/video-compressor/*
  ! Content-Security-Policy
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; img-src 'self' data: blob:; media-src 'self' blob:; font-src 'self' data:; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' 'wasm-unsafe-eval' blob: https://cdn.jsdelivr.net; worker-src 'self' blob:; connect-src 'self' https://cdn.jsdelivr.net; manifest-src 'self'
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp

# OCR: tesseract.js is used with its default (CDN) worker/core/language-data
# paths — see src/tools/ocr/Ocr.svelte, no override is passed to
# createWorker() — so its script, worker and wasm all come from jsdelivr.
# NOT given COOP/COEP: tesseract.js's jsdelivr-hosted core does not send a
# Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy header, which COEP:require-corp would block.
/ocr/*
  ! Content-Security-Policy
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; img-src 'self' data: blob:; media-src 'self' blob:; font-src 'self' data:; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' 'wasm-unsafe-eval' https://cdn.jsdelivr.net; worker-src 'self' blob: https://cdn.jsdelivr.net; connect-src 'self' https://cdn.jsdelivr.net; manifest-src 'self'

# Transcriber: @huggingface/transformers fetches Whisper model weights from
# Hugging Face and, since no wasmPaths override is set in Transcriber.svelte,
# falls back to jsdelivr for its internal onnxruntime-web WASM backend too.
# `blob:` in script-src is required for the same reason as
# /remove-background/* and /image-upscaler/* below: onnxruntime-web
# dynamically `import()`s its fetched core as a `blob:` URL.
/transcribe/*
  ! Content-Security-Policy
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; img-src 'self' data: blob:; media-src 'self' blob:; font-src 'self' data:; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' 'wasm-unsafe-eval' blob: https://cdn.jsdelivr.net; worker-src 'self' blob: https://cdn.jsdelivr.net; connect-src 'self' https://huggingface.co https://*.hf.co https://cdn.jsdelivr.net; manifest-src 'self'

# File Drop: WebRTC signaling. PUBLIC_SIGNALING_URL (build-time env var,
# src/tools/file-drop/FileDrop.svelte) can point at either the custom domain
# (wss://signal.tools.nabl.in, once that route is set up in
# workers/filedrop/wrangler.toml) or the Worker's default
# *.workers.dev URL — both are allowed here so neither deploy path needs a
# _headers change. `wss://*.workers.dev` matches the two-label
# <worker-name>.<account-subdomain>.workers.dev host Cloudflare assigns by
# default (confirmed live in real Chromium: the CSP wildcard matches
# multi-label subdomains, not just one label). Until either is deployed,
# it falls back to same-origin wss://<host>/ws/filedrop, already covered by
# 'self'. The public STUN server (stun:stun.l.google.com:19302) used for ICE
# negotiation is deliberately NOT listed in connect-src: tested live and
# confirmed Chrome rejects "stun:host:port" as an invalid CSP source-list
# entry (STUN URIs use a bare scheme:host:port, not CSP's scheme://host:port
# grammar) — it's silently dropped from the policy with a console warning,
# so including it does nothing. connect-src does not gate WebRTC ICE/STUN
# candidate gathering in current Chrome regardless, so no source-list entry
# is needed for it to keep working.
/file-drop/*
  ! Content-Security-Policy
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; img-src 'self' data: blob:; media-src 'self' blob:; font-src 'self' data:; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' 'wasm-unsafe-eval'; worker-src 'self' blob:; connect-src 'self' wss://signal.tools.nabl.in wss://*.workers.dev; manifest-src 'self'

# Camera / microphone / screen-capture permissions, scoped to only the tool
# pages whose Svelte components actually call getUserMedia/getDisplayMedia
# (verified against every src/tools/*/*.svelte — see the audit report).
# Transcriber takes file upload only (no getUserMedia call in its source),
# so it is deliberately left off this list.
/webcam-test/*
  ! Permissions-Policy
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(self), microphone=(), display-capture=(), geolocation=(), payment=()

/mic-test/*
  ! Permissions-Policy
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(self), display-capture=(), geolocation=(), payment=()

/screen-recorder/*
  ! Permissions-Policy
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(self), microphone=(self), display-capture=(self), geolocation=(), payment=()
